// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! D-METHODMACRO1=A: checked `#Inline` / `#Inline(Always)` contracts.
//RS //!
//RS //! `#Inline` is a soft hint — never rejected here, never even inspected by
//RS //! this module. `#Inline(Always)` is a checked promise: if the compiler can
//RS //! prove it genuinely cannot inline the call, that's a compile error naming
//RS //! why (never a silent miss). Three ways a function fails the promise:
//RS //!
//RS //!   - **E0917** self-recursive — inlining a call to itself has no fixed
//RS //!     expansion (would loop forever at compile time or need an artificial
//RS //!     depth cutoff). Checked here: a direct call/method-call to the
//RS //!     function's own name anywhere in its straight-line/control-flow body.
//RS //!     Coverage note: only DIRECT self-recursion is checked (a function
//RS //!     calling itself by name). Mutual recursion between two `#Inline(Always)`
//RS //!     functions is NOT checked — that needs a whole-program call graph,
//RS //!     which nothing in sema builds *before* per-function checking runs (the
//RS //!     effect-summary call graph in `Effects.rs` is only complete *after*
//RS //!     every function has been checked once). Out of scope for this card;
//RS //!     flagged here rather than silently narrowed.
//RS //!   - **E0918** address-taken — the function's bare name is used as a VALUE
//RS //!     anywhere in the program (stored in a binding, passed as a callback,
//RS //!     returned), not just called directly. Checked via `inline_addr_taken`,
//RS //!     a whole-program accumulator threaded through `check_func_body`'s
//RS //!     body products (see `Checker::inline_addr_taken`) and
//RS //!     populated for free (`CheckerInfer/expr.rs`'s `Expr::Ident` arm already
//RS //!     visits every expression in every function during ordinary type
//RS //!     inference; the one line that resolves a bare name to a global
//RS //!     function's signature is exactly "this name was read as a value").
//RS //!     Methods can't appear in this set — Jet's grammar has no way to take a
//RS //!     method's address as a bare value — so E0918 only ever fires for
//RS //!     top-level functions.
//RS //!   - **E0919** too large — the body exceeds `INLINE_ALWAYS_MAX_STMTS`
//RS //!     statements (counted transitively through nested blocks — `if`/`loop`/
//RS //!     `switch`/etc — but NOT through a nested `Lambda` body, which compiles
//RS //!     to its own separate closure, not inline text of this function).
//RS //!
//RS //! I3: this module only decides; `crates/jet-codegen` emits `#[inline]` /
//RS //! `#[inline(always)]` purely off `Func::is_inline`/`is_inline_always` once
//RS //! this check (and the rest of sema) has passed.
//RS 
//RS use crate::Diagnostics::{Diagnostic, Span};
